weighing his strengths, and that C's positive crew atmosphere and reliability may be more important. Or we could argue that C's communication difficulty and egocentric attitude are also serious. Need to decide.\n\nGiven the panel hasn't fully discussed D, but we have limited info. Perhaps we can argue that Candidate C's positive crew atmosphere and reliability outweigh B's uncooperative remarks, and that communication difficulty may be mitigated. So we could shift vote to C.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 2 argued B still best; Agent 1 and Agent 2 earlier gave concerns about C. We can point out that B's uncooperative behavior is not just \"grumpy\" but \"makes nasty remarks\", which could severely impact cockpit safety. Meanwhile C creates positive atmosphere, despite communication difficulty. Also C is 100% reliable and makes correct decisions quickly. Those are critical. So we could change vote to C.\n\nWe need to provide evidence: C 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, correct decisions quickly. B's uncooperative behavior: \"makes nasty remarks\", \"grumpy\", \"uncooperative\". Also B's strengths: stress handling, conscientiousness, weather assessment, computer skills. But crew cooperation is essential. So we argue that C's crew cooperation is stronger.\n\nThus we will change vote to Candidate C.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: from notes and discussion. Provide reasoning.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
